<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,279.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose four points to 1,279.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,279 today from 1,275 on May 9, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate	Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1360    12.350	  1358    12.331</p>
<p>   1a   1292  9788.000	  1282  9713.000</p>
<p>   2    1522    21.750	  1519    21.706</p>
<p>   2a   1532 12563.000	  1520 12469.000</p>
<p>   3    1362    12.563	  1356    12.513</p>
<p>   3a   1170  9238.000	  1161  9163.000</p>
<p>   6    1217    12.556	  1223    12.619</p>
<p>   7    1151     5.606	  1153     5.613</p>
<p>   8     876     9.638	   879     9.669</p>
<p>   9     721  6306.000	   712  6225.000</p>
<p>  10    1106     5.588	  1111     5.613</p>
